WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:05.040
Film Courage: Jen, can you provide some advice
for writers coming out of college?

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.640
Maybe these individuals have been told “You’re
amazing!

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.740
You’re going to set the world on fire…You’re
going to leave our little school.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:17.930
Good luck!” and off they go…Jen Grisanti:
I would say the biggest advice to writers

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:22.050
coming out of college is live your life.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:30.880
Like when writers go straight from college
to the writer’s room and not experience

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:37.969
life, then I find that they are stunted.

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:45.690
I mean for me personally, I like the writer
who explores another career path and comes

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:53.320
into the writing and succeeds or fails miserably
and has something to say.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:01:00.059
Like that to me is more interesting than the
writer who got straight A’s all the way

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:04.110
through school and then goes into the writer’s
room.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:14.940
So I think the biggest thing is understand
the journey as well.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:21.820
Understand that it’s not about selling that
first script.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:31.630
It’s about creating longevity and it’s
about really taking the time to grow into

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:39.180
your own skin, understand who you are, what
you have to say, and the impact you want to

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:42.340
make on the world with your writing.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:47.140
Film Courage: So then let’s suppose they
are [this hypothetical writer] several years

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:52.231
out of college and they finally say “I am
going to block out this much time to write

00:01:52.231 --> 00:01:54.180
this amazing script.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.390
What should I start writing about?

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:59.950
Should I write a horror film, because I know
those [movies] are popular with the 18-34

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:04.270
demographic and I know I can add a soundtrack
to it…”

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:10.590
Jen Grisanti: I would say write what you are
the most passionate about.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:15.780
You have to recognize that the number one
thing that sells is passion.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:24.620
And as much as you can say that this genre
sells as much as this genre, the timing for

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:32.450
this genre might be better, but if the passion
isn’t there, it will show up on the page.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:41.641
And I think if there were an exact science
as to what will hit then writers would be

00:02:41.641 --> 00:02:43.210
making it all over the place.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:49.020
I think really…like I’m going to tell
you from being a studio executive from the

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:57.460
number of years that I was and still being
a writing instructor at NBC and studying pilots

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:04.330
and knowing that Hollywood doesn’t exactly
know what’s going to hit.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:12.120
Like they’re throwing it out there and praying
that Middle America is going to show up.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:20.280
And you can have…I think if you were going
to survey a bunch of studio executives at

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:27.170
the beginning of each season and say what
shows do you think are going to be the breakout

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:33.720
hits versus what shows are not, because you
know it’s hit or miss.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:39.099
Film Courage: So going back to this writer
coming out of college and they proclaim “I

00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:44.660
love [the show] LOST and I am going to write
another version of it…but that is not anything

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:49.040
like what their personal story is about.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.880
And you get to know this person and you find
they had a totally different life from like…I

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:57.660
mean being on an island is not something most
people have experienced but something that

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:00.400
is very dissimilar to what they want to write
about.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.599
What do you say?

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:08.070
Jen Grisanti: I always say the best thing
to write right now is something that connects

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:09.850
to your emotional truth.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:18.239
So if you are dying to write something that
has no link to your emotional truth then think

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:23.529
about why you’re passionate about the concept.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:30.999
And maybe move for…like I’ve helped writers
think of personal stories that they didn’t

00:04:30.999 --> 00:04:35.819
realize actually did connect to the concept.

00:04:35.819 --> 00:04:44.910
I definitely think that there are writers
who function better writing about things that

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:48.180
are removed from them.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:54.949
But what you have to think about…like say
when you take Harry Potter, you ground it

00:04:54.949 --> 00:05:07.059
in thematic emotion and the idea of what does
ground the concept.

00:05:07.059 --> 00:05:15.900
Those are themes of childhood and coming into
your own and things that we all connect with

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.110
on a massive level.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:25.779
Like when I covered The 4400 I remember thinking
“Okay, not many of us are going to relate

00:05:25.779 --> 00:05:32.159
to The 4400 that were abducted from earth
and then returned back to a life that moved

00:05:32.159 --> 00:05:33.159
on.

00:05:33.159 --> 00:05:45.379
But what we identify with is abandonment,
redefining your life, the idea with failure

00:05:45.379 --> 00:05:49.009
to reconnect with family that has moved on.

00:05:49.009 --> 00:05:51.930
There are all those things we connect with.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:58.499
So I think when you’re writing stories that
are outside your emotional truth, figuring

00:05:58.499 --> 00:06:04.919
out how to ground them so that even though
the concept may be way outside anything you

00:06:04.919 --> 00:06:07.990
know, the emotion and the themes are connected.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:08.990
Question for the Viewers: What’s the best
writing advice you have received in the last

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:08.992
12 months

